  clock: 6  # 609d
  nonce: 609d  # 609d
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-08-27. Merged as PR #564, dev SHA 46ca2dc35394. Evidence is the ITEM OWN FILED REPRO re-run on the MERGED tree, with two controls in the same run.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO, verbatim from the description, before/after:\n\n    std::fs::File kinds TODAY: [function]        starved: []\n    after adding File::metadata as a method:     starved: []\n\nThe second line is the one that moved. As filed it read starved: [std::fs::File]\n-- ONE CORRECT ROW FLIPPING A CLEAN VERDICT TO A WITHHELD ONE. WI-bupor can now\nadd the File methods without regressing every Rust repo that opens a file.\n\nNote the repro edge is UNSTAMPED (no call_construct), because that is what the\nanalyzer really emits for an associated-function call to an external type. The\nconstruct route alone does NOT close this repro; the NAME route does. That is\nwhy the fix has two routes and not one.\n\nTWO CONTROLS IN THE SAME RUN, both of which must still starve, and both do:\n  * kotlin java.io.File, constructor call only  -> [java.io.File]\n    The blind-language population this gate exists for is untouched.\n  * std::path::Path, unstamped Path::new        -> [std::path::Path]\n    INV-linub L3 slot-external defect is NOT papered over by this change.\n\nWithout these the run could have been blind and the first line would look\nidentical either way -- evidence for FIXED and for NOTHING REACHED THE GATE is\nthe same at the output.\n\nCORPUS MEASUREMENT, already recorded above and unchanged by the merge: 42 real\nrepos, 6 modules freed today, 7 once WI-bupor lands, empty new-starvation set\neverywhere, every freed module mixed-kind.\n\nONE PROCESS FINDING WORTH CARRYING. The coverage gate, not the assertions,\ncaught that NO test executed the name route: every test in the mixed-kind class\nstamps call_construct, so the route whose entire justification is unstamped\nedges had never run. Six tests were added and line 3084 confirmed EXECUTED\nrather than merely green. A PASSING SUITE IS NOT AN EXERCISED BRANCH."  # 609d
